---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Bar · The Renewal · OASTL"
  description="A pro bono panel of lawyers for school-trust law, in formation. The law is built and organized; the on-ramp is open now."
  path="/renewal/bar/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The Renewal · The Bar"
    title="The gift’s next generation of defenders."
    dek="The trusts are perpetual, but their defenders are not. Every generation of beneficiaries needs its own lawyers."
  />

  <section class="bg-oastl-bone">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
      <div class="space-y-4 text-[17px] text-oastl-ink/85 leading-relaxed font-serif">
        <p>
          School-trust law is real, winnable, and two centuries deep. It is also a field with a structural problem: the trusts are perpetual, but their defenders are not. Every generation of beneficiaries needs its own lawyers, and most generations have gone without — not because the claims were weak, but because no one had gathered the law, and every new advocate had to start from nothing.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Bar exists to end that. It will be a pro bono panel of trial and appellate lawyers, researchers, and law students who take up the defense of the school trusts — equipped from day one, so that no member ever starts from scratch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-oastl-cream/40 border-y border-oastl-forest/15">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
      <div class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-oastl-forest mb-2">
        The kit
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-oastl-forest font-semibold leading-tight">
        What a member of the panel gets.
      </h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 list-disc pl-5 text-[16px] text-oastl-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
        <li>
          <strong>The hornbook</strong> — a complete first-draft treatise of school-trust law, nineteen chapters with a state appendix for each of the twenty trust-land states, published by <a href="https://schooltrusts.net/writing/hornbook/" class="underline decoration-oastl-gold/60 hover:text-oastl-gold">America’s School Trust Library</a> and free to read.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The public case-law catalog</strong> — the case-law gateways for these trusts are kept by America’s School Trust Library, a separate institution that takes no position in litigation. Its own <a href="https://schooltrusts.net/workshop/" class="underline decoration-oastl-gold/60 hover:text-oastl-gold">workshop page</a> reports <strong>220 files held and 19 public so far</strong>. The public ones sit in the Library’s <a href="https://schooltrusts.net/catalog/" class="underline decoration-oastl-gold/60 hover:text-oastl-gold">catalog</a>, which anyone may consult; the rest are not yet released, and the panel has no privileged access to them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The Oregon case record</strong> — OASTL is a party in active Oregon school-trust litigation, and the complaint, the rulings, the appellate opinion, and the other public filings are gathered on the <a href="/legal-desk/" class="underline decoration-oastl-gold/60 hover:text-oastl-gold">OASTL Legal Desk</a>. Panel members work from a live record and from lawyers who have argued it, not from a hypothetical.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Model materials</strong> — briefing architecture and <a href="/renewal/act/text/" class="underline decoration-oastl-gold/60 hover:text-oastl-gold">model legislation</a> to work from rather than reinvent.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-oastl-bone">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
      <div class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-oastl-forest mb-2">
        Who runs it
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-oastl-forest font-semibold leading-tight">
        Owned by the cause, not by a bar association.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[17px] text-oastl-ink/85 leading-relaxed font-serif">
        <p>
          The panel is organized by Oregon Advocates for School Trust Lands, which runs the Renewal today; a dedicated nonprofit home for the program is still in formation. It is deliberately independent — owned by the cause, not by any bar association. The panel’s public details will be announced here when they are ready; this page will stay spare until then.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-oastl-forest mt-12 mb-2">
        The on-ramp
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-oastl-forest font-semibold leading-tight">
        The on-ramp is open now.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[17px] text-oastl-ink/85 leading-relaxed font-serif">
        <p>
          You don’t have to wait for the formal panel. The law is already built and free to read — start with the lawyer’s entrance to America’s School Trust Library and the hornbook itself. If the work speaks to you, raise your hand: write to <strong>Dave Sullivan, president of OASTL</strong>, at <a href="mailto:drdavesullivan@gmail.com?subject=Pro%20bono%20%E2%80%94%20count%20me%20in" class="underline decoration-oastl-gold/60 hover:text-oastl-gold">drdavesullivan@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Allies who aren’t lawyers are welcome too. Legal librarians, researchers, and archivists have a standing invitation at the Library’s <a href="https://schooltrusts.net/librarians/" class="underline decoration-oastl-gold/60 hover:text-oastl-gold">librarians’ entrance</a> — an invitation from that institution, not from OASTL.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="mailto:drdavesullivan@gmail.com?subject=Pro%20bono%20%E2%80%94%20count%20me%20in"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-oastl-forest text-oastl-cream px-5 py-3 rounded-sm font-medium hover:bg-oastl-canopy"
        >
          I’m a lawyer — count me in →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://schooltrusts.net/for-lawyers/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-oastl-forest/30 text-oastl-forest px-5 py-3 rounded-sm font-medium hover:border-oastl-gold"
        >
          Read the law →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://schooltrusts.net/writing/hornbook/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-oastl-forest/30 text-oastl-forest px-5 py-3 rounded-sm font-medium hover:border-oastl-gold"
        >
          The hornbook →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/renewal/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-oastl-forest/30 text-oastl-forest px-5 py-3 rounded-sm font-medium hover:border-oastl-gold"
        >
          Return to the Renewal
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
